WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.816 --> 00:00:04.530
♪ Nilay's Chemistry ♪

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.930
- Let's start off with a problem.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.480
A person drops a pound of bricks

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.627
and a pound of feathers
down from their window,

00:00:12.627 --> 00:00:17.610
which has more matter?
The bricks or the feathers?

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.460
Now, you might be tempted to say feathers

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.463
but let's recall what matter is.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:29.280
Matter is anything that
occupies space and has mass.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.900
Mass defines the quantity
of matter in an object.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.370
Mass tells us when we have a
lot of matter like an elephant

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:42.240
or only a little bit
of matter like a mouse.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.350
So back to the problem,
which has more matter?

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.040
A pound of bricks or a pound of feathers?

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.760
Well, they both have a mass of one pound

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.463
so they have the same amount of matter.

00:00:57.441 --> 00:01:02.280
Now, even though bricks and
feathers are very different,

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.010
they're both made up of matter.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:08.613
But what exactly is matter made up of?

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.760
Matter is made up of one

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.710
or many microscopic building
blocks called atoms.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.520
An atom is the smallest unit of matter

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.500
and they are so tiny

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.420
that a penny contains
approximately 2.3 times 10

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.363
to the 22nd atoms, or 23 sextillion atoms.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.880
However, all of the sextillions

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.420
of atoms in a penny aren't the same.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.560
A penny is made up of
copper and zinc atoms.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.186
Copper and zinc are just two examples

00:01:46.186 --> 00:01:51.186
of the 118 different elements that exist.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.824
An element is a substance
that cannot be decomposed

00:01:54.824 --> 00:01:58.593
into a simpler substance
by chemical means.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.370
Essentially, if you have an element,

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:06.904
no reaction with heat or another
chemical can break it down

00:02:06.904 --> 00:02:09.570
into a simpler substance.

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.840
Hydrogen, oxygen, carbon, gold,

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:16.773
and arsenic are all different elements.

00:02:16.773 --> 00:02:20.040
When you have a sample of an element,

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.510
it can consist of one or more atoms.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:29.100
So, elemental neon exists
as a singular, free atom,

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:33.480
which does not interact
with any other atoms.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.170
Elemental gold usually exists as millions

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.910
or trillions of connected
atoms while oxygen exists

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:46.893
in a diatomic molecular
form with two oxygen atoms.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:52.650
Oxygen in its elemental form
is an example of a molecule

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:57.150
because its two atoms are
chemically bound together.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.360
A molecule is the smallest physical unit

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:05.360
of an element or compound, and
it is anything made up of two

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:09.273
or more atoms held together
by a chemical bond.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:14.190
So if atoms are held together by bonds

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:18.360
then it also makes sense that
these bonds can be broken

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:22.320
and allow different atoms
to then bond together.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.320
Almost like Lego blocks,
for example, water

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:32.750
or H2O comprises two hydrogen
atoms and one oxygen atom.

00:03:34.197 --> 00:03:38.790
In this chemical reaction, hydrogen or H2

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:43.770
and oxygen or O2 react to form water.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.660
The chemical bonds holding

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.560
the diatomic oxygen
molecules together are broken

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.376
so that each oxygen atom can then bond

00:03:52.376 --> 00:03:56.490
with two hydrogen atoms.
By rearranging the way

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.860
that atoms are attached to one another.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:02.700
Reactions like this can
occur where one molecule

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.640
is transformed into another.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:09.450
A good analogy is that
atoms are like letters

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.820
and molecules are like words.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:15.270
If we change the order or type of letter,

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:18.960
we make different words
with different meanings.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.650
If we change the order or type of atom,

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:26.193
we make different molecules
with different properties.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.720
So let's summarize what we have learned.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.210
Matter is made up of atoms

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.550
and we can obtain different types

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.985
of matter from objects being
built with different elements.

00:04:39.985 --> 00:04:44.026
So while a pound of bricks
and a pound of feathers

00:04:44.026 --> 00:04:47.400
have the same amount
of matter, they're made

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.820
of different elemental
building blocks called atoms

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:54.120
that then give them different properties.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.510
This is why a pound of
bricks dropping down

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:01.893
from above is a lot scarier
than a pound of feathers. 

00:05:02.766 --> 00:05:06.349
♪ Nilay's Chemistry Videos ♪

